e Endnote (file)\nexport refworks Refworks\n\nRequest / recall this title\n(2-3 business days)\n[Cover--Click to expand.]\n[Add this title to your marked items list]\nAdd\nPerforming an archive\nSuzy Lake.\nAuthor: \tLake, Suzy, photographer.\nPublished: \tMontréal : Dazibao ; London, UK : Black Dog Publishing, 2015.\nDescription: \t1 volume (unnumbered) : color illustrations ; 22 cm.\nFormat: \tBook\nSummary:\nIn Performing an Archive , Suzy Lake, an essential figure in Canadian contemporary art with an international reputation, continues her exploration of questions around identity and social issues. Drawi ng on history and her own family chronicle, Lake bears witness to the urban, demographic and social development of Detroit, a city marked throughout the twentieth century by economic decline, racial tension and a startling crime rate. In a performative process, she visits the scene of various locations where her ancestors lived.\n\nBorn in Detroit, Michigan, Suzy Lake has lived in Canada since the late 1960s, where she widely contributed to the emergence of conceptual and feminist art. She was one of the first artists in Canada to use performance, video and photography to explore questions of gender, the body and identity. Her work has been shown in numerous major exhibitions, including WACK! Art and the Feminist Revolution (organised by the Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art, 2007), Suzy Lake: Political Poetics (organised by the University of Toronto Art Centre and the Scotiabank CONTACT Photography Festival, 2011) and Traffic: Conceptual Art in Canada 1965-1980 (organised by the Art Gallery of Alberta, the Justina M Barnicke Gallery at University of Toronto and the Vancouver Art Gallery, in partnership with the Leonard and Bina Ellen Gallery at Concordia University and Halifax, INK, 2012), exhibitions which later circulated widely. In 2014, the Art Gallery of Ontario mounted a major retrospective of her work, Introducing Suzy Lake. She has been a member of the Royal Canadian Academy of Arts since 2004.\nContent provided by Syndetic Solutions, Inc. Terms of Use\n... ( see more )\n\n    Subjects\n    Location\n    MARC\n    Full Record\n\nSubjects\nLake, Suzy.\nPhotography, Artistic -- 21st century.\nPhotography -- Canada -- 21st century.\n\nUniform Title: \tLake, Suzy, Photographs. Selections\nVarying Title: \tSuzy Lake : performing an archive\nOther Author: \tDazibao (Art gallery), issuing body.\nSeries: \tLes portables\nSeries: \tPortables (Dazibao (Art gallery))\nLocation\nOnline\nLocation \tCall # \tStatus \tNotes\nArt Library \tTR655 .L352 2015 \tAvailable \t\nArt Library \tTR655 .L352 2015 \tAvailable \t\nMARC\nLEADER 00000cam a2200481Ii 4500 \n001    913176342 \n003    OCoLC \n005    20160210031604.0 \n008    150625s2015    quca          000 0 eng d \n019    913337784 \n020    9781910433676|q(Black Dog Publishing) \n020    1910433675|q(Black Dog Publishing) \n020    9782922135435|q(Dazibao) \n020    2922135438|q(Dazibao) \n035    (OCoLC)913176342|z(OCoLC)913337784 \n040    CaQMBN|beng|erda|cNLC|dOCLCO|dYDXCP|dBTCTA|dBDX|dEYM\n       |dNMWMA|dZCU|dNOC \n041 0  eng|afre \n049    NOCC \n050  4 TR655|b.L352 2015 \n055  3 TR647|bL35 2015 \n100 1  Lake, Suzy,|ephotographer. \n240 10 Photographs.|kSelections \n245 10 Performing an archive /|cSuzy Lake. \n246 3  Suzy Lake :|bperforming an archive \n264  1 Montréal :|bDazibao ;|aLondon, UK :|bBlack Dog Publishing,\n       |c2015. \n300    1 volume (unnumbered) :|bcolor illustrations ;|c22 cm. \n336    text|btxt|2rdacontent \n336    still image|bsti|2rdacontent \n337    unmediated|bn|2rdamedia \n338    volume|bnc|2rdacarrier \n490 1  Les portables \n546    Text in French and English. \n600 10 Lake, Suzy. \n650  0 Photography, Artistic|y21st century. \n650  0 Photography|zCanada|y21st century. \n710 2  Dazibao (Art gallery),|eissuing body. \n830  0 Portables (Dazibao (Art gallery)) \n915    |9Under Authority Control \n949  1 TR655|b.L352 2015|z050 4|g1|i00049918080|laada|